{
  "id": "ss.enemy.bristle",
  "name": "Bristle",
  "description": "The burrow's fast chaff — a silverfish out of the wall seams, running the nest's trails and stealing off them, the one thing down here that does not belong to the hive. Drawn from the side and mirrored by the game, like the rest of the roster: an earlier cut was top-down so the game could turn it to its heading, and a body drawn side-on cannot be turned — it would walk lying on its side. The three caudal filaments are one fused plume rather than three rods, because five thin rods radiating off a small oval is an asterisk at the size this is seen at and not a creature; the notches keep them legible as three. The fan is four layers — three outlines of falling size with the hairs drawn across them — plus three filaments escaping past the edge so it is not a clean curve. All of it is rooted at one point behind the abdomen, which is why it sweeps on one rotation per layer, each arriving later than the one outside it: the plume lagging the body that drags it is the whole motion, and nothing rooted together can come apart. The silhouette is a comet, which nothing else here is. Cool silver against a roster of warm bone and amber so it never competes with the Replete or the Porter's brood, and the palest body on it — this runs on #372d3f earth and the quickest thing on screen must not be the hardest to see. Gameplay radius 7.",
